{{Finnish index|m|u}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from a {{etyl|gem|fi}} language, compare {{m|und||myra}}, or from {{inh|ru|ine-pro|*moruiH-}}, compare Ukrainian {{m|uk||мура́ха}}.

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# An [[ant]].

====Usage notes====
* In compounds where {{m|fi||muurahainen}} functions as a modifier, it contracts to the form {{m|fi|muurahais-||ant-, form-, myrmeco-}}.

